3. Precompiled Schematron rule sets (schematron/**/*.sef.json)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The .sef.json files are the original Schematron rules compiled to the SaxonJS
stylesheet export format (SEF), with two small, documented workarounds for
SaxonJS 2.7 (see schematron/SOURCE.md). They are modified (compiled) forms of
the works named below and are distributed under the license of the respective
original. They are separate data files that the library loads at runtime; they
are not linked into or merged with this project's code.

3.1 EN 16931 CII validation artefacts, version 1.3.16 (CEN/TC 434)
    Published by the European Commission / ConnectingEurope.
    Source: https://github.com/ConnectingEurope/eInvoicing-EN16931
            (release validation-1.3.16, asset en16931-cii-1.3.16.zip)
    License: European Union Public Licence (EUPL) version 1.2.
    Text: licenses/EUPL-1.2.txt
    Files: schematron/en16931/EN16931-CII-validation.sef.json
    Source code availability (EUPL, Article 5): the original XSLT, the
    compilation script and the compiled files are available in the Git
    repository https://github.com/Itegro-GmbH/einvoice under schematron/en16931/
    and scripts/compile-sef.mjs; the upstream source is at the link above.

3.2 XRechnung 3.0.2 Schematron, version 2.6.0 (KoSIT)
    Published by the Koordinierungsstelle fuer IT-Standards (KoSIT).
    Source: https://github.com/itplr-kosit/xrechnung-schematron
            (release v2.6.0, asset xrechnung-3.0.2-schematron-2.6.0.zip)
    License: Apache License, Version 2.0.
    Text: schematron/xrechnung/LICENSE-Apache-2.0.txt (the upstream license file,
    unchanged; it also contains the upstream note on the reproduction of the
    EN 16931 based data model by permission of CEN and DIN). The upstream
    repository contains no NOTICE file.
    Files: schematron/xrechnung/XRechnung-CII-validation.sef.json

3.3 Factur-X / ZUGFeRD Schematron rule sets: NOT included
    The rule sets published by FNFE-MPE and FeRD for the Factur-X / ZUGFeRD
    profiles BASIC, EN 16931 and EXTENDED carry no license statement that
    permits redistribution (the publishers' site reserves all rights and the
    original packages are only available behind a registration form), so they
    are neither part of the repository nor of the npm package. They are downloaded from their public source and compiled
    on your machine when you run "npx einvoice-setup-facturx" (see README).

